WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.329
On this Records screen, Drafts and Recent show different

00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:05.010
parts of an entry’s progress.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.739
Find the training entry in Drafts and compare its descriptive

00:00:08.739 --> 00:00:10.010
text before opening it.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:14.090
The reference beginning with D identifies this draft; it is

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.920
not yet the final record number.

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:20.030
Open that entry, keeping it distinct from the separate Work draft.

00:00:20.239 --> 00:00:24.489
The opened form is Training Only, Community software exercise.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.309
In Details, Summary is marked required, and Notes provides space

00:00:29.309 --> 00:00:30.840
for the supporting explanation.

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:34.699
Read the existing Summary first so you can recognize this record

00:00:34.699 --> 00:00:36.010
when you return to the list.

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:40.000
The Notes currently describe a fictional Resgrid form exercise.

00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:44.940
Under Attachments, Take a photo, Choose a photo and Choose a file

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:49.299
are available, while No attachments yet shows this example has none.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:54.050
Update Notes with the information that belongs in this entry, then choose Save.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.809
Here, the revised Notes explain that the department form was

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:01.769
reviewed in Responder and that this is a software practice exercise.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.560
The app returns Saved, and the record still shows Draft.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.829
Keep the unchanged Summary and draft reference in view so you can tell this

00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:11.739
revision belongs to the same record.

00:01:11.949 --> 00:01:15.920
When you reopen the same draft from the Records list, read Notes again.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.140
The revised software exercise text is retained here, rather than

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.180
only sitting in an unsaved editor.

00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:25.869
No attachments yet remains the actual attachment state.

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:29.460
Before completing the record, compare the saved content with

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.190
the work you actually documented.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:35.640
Read the statement, I attest this Record is complete and accurate.

00:01:35.999 --> 00:01:39.830
The checkbox is initially empty, and Finalize is unavailable.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:44.509
Select the attestation only after checking the record’s actual content.

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:49.030
In this example, that content describes a fictional software exercise.

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:52.860
With the attestation selected, Finalize becomes available.

00:01:53.019 --> 00:01:56.229
Choose Finalize once when this record is ready to complete.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.760
The app returns Finalized and displays a final record number at the top

00:02:00.849 --> 00:02:02.529
in place of the draft reference.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:06.999
Summary and Notes are now read-only, and the attachment-picking actions

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:08.680
are no longer offered in this view.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:11.970
This is the observed completion of this record, rather than

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.509
a submitted review request.

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:16.379
Use Back to return to the Records workspace.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.710
In Recent, find the same descriptive text together with its final

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.900
record number and Finalized status.

00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:26.620
The separate Work draft remains in Drafts, while the entry you

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.669
completed is no longer listed there.

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:32.590
Reopen that Recent entry and confirm its number, Finalized

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.700
status, Summary and Notes.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:39.140
This fresh readback retains the saved content, and Save, Submit

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.449
for review and Finalize are absent from the completed form.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:46.859
Use the same identity, save and final-readback checks for forms

00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:50.380
used by community paramedicine and mental health teams, search and

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:55.189
rescue, security companies, wildland contractors, industrial responders

00:02:55.279 --> 00:02:57.220
and fire or EMS departments.

00:02:57.609 --> 00:03:01.400
Choose the content appropriate to your department, and verify each record’s

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.359
actual state before leaving it.
